<article class="env-proposition" id="8013FE">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/8013FE">Proposition <span data-tag="8013FE">3.2.1.14</span>.</a> For any marked simplicial set $M = (X, \calE )$, the natural map $|X|_{Q^{\bullet }} \rightarrow X$ induces a Cartesian equivalence </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  T(M) \rightarrow M. \]
</div>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      As in the proof of Proposition <a href="/tag/71BCFE" data-tag="71BCFE">3.2.1.13</a>, we may reduce to the case where $M$ consists of a simplex of dimension $\leq 1$ (either marked or unmarked). In these cases, the map $T(M) \rightarrow M$ is an isomorphism in $\mSet $. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>